            "topic": "KPMG Australia: 387 job cuts and 13% partner pay drop after audit leaks scandal",
            "summary": "KPMG Australia is cutting 27 partners and about 360 staff (~5% of its workforce) and slashing average equity partner pay 13% to A$645,000, after a whistleblower scandal over misused Lendlease board papers wiped out consulting work and cost it its CEO, its federal contract pipeline and major audit clients. FY26 revenue slipped 1% to A$2.26bn while consulting fell 17% to A$632m.",
