            "keyPoints": [
                "The trigger: a whistleblower alleged confidential Lendlease board papers were used to chase Westpac and Dexus audit tenders.",
                "Labor senator Deborah O'Neill read the allegations into parliament under privilege in March 2026.",
                "KPMG's first internal investigation found nothing; law firm Allens was later brought in externally.",
                "CEO Andrew Yates resigned 29 May 2026; the COO and other senior partners also left.",
                "ASIC escalated from preliminary inquiries to a formal investigation of KPMG and three registered auditors.",
                "Canberra paused new KPMG contracts for procurements closing 16 June–30 September 2026, pending a governance review.",
                "Consulting revenue is now A$632m, down from more than A$1bn three years earlier.",
                "Macquarie reversed its plan to appoint KPMG and kept PwC as auditor on 26 August 2026.",
                "Treasury is consulting on splitting Big Four audit and consulting arms and capping partnerships at 400 partners.",
                "KPMG expects subdued economic conditions to persist to at least 2028."
